course: dictionary
lesson: 4170
title: Goblins, made-up and real
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A goblin is a small, ugly, mischievous creature from fairy tales and fantasy stories. Goblins are often green or grey, with pointy ears, and they cause trouble, steal, and guard treasure in caves or under hills. Read the clues around the word to work out which kind of goblin is meant.
explain: «The goblin shark of the deep sea is pink because its blood shows through its thin skin.» This goblin is not a made-up creature. It is a real fish, and the sentence tells you so with «deep sea» and «its blood». The name is borrowed from the fairy-tale goblin, probably because the shark looks strange and a little scary.
explain: Context also shows you when goblin is used as a joke. If a grandad smiles and says «you little goblin», he is not calling you a creature. He means you are being naughty, or sneaky about grabbing a biscuit. Ask yourself: is the word about a creature, a real animal, or a playful tease?
fact: A goblin is a made-up creature in fairy tales and fantasy stories.
fact: Goblins are usually shown as small, ugly, mischievous, and often green or grey, with pointy ears.
fact: «Goblin» can also be a fond, informal word for a naughty child or someone acting greedily or sneakily.
fact: «The goblin shark's family goes back over 100 million years, so it is sometimes called a living fossil.»
fact: A living fossil is an animal that looks much like its ancient relatives, and few people have seen one alive.
exercise: «The goblin shark of the deep sea is pink because its blood shows through its thin skin.» Why is the goblin shark pink? | *Its blood shows through its thin skin | It was painted by fishermen | It lives in a pink cave under a hill | It eats only pink food
exercise: Dad smiles and says, «You little goblin!» What does he mean? | *You are being naughty, in a playful way | You are the king of the castle | You are a made-up creature from a fairy tale | You are a shark from the deep sea
exercise: «The goblin shark's family goes back over 100 million years.» Find and copy the words that show the shark is very old. | goblin shark | deep sea | *over 100 million years | few people
test: In fairy tales, what is a goblin usually shown with? | Wings and a golden halo | *Pointy ears and green or grey skin | Scales and a long fin | A long white beard and a hat
test: Why is the goblin shark called a living fossil? | *Its family goes back over 100 million years | It lives in a museum | It has been turned to stone | It is made of bone
exam: Goblins are made-up creatures in stories, but what is the goblin shark? | *A real fish that lives in the deep sea | A made-up creature from a fairy tale | A goblin who runs a bank | A naughty child
